{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And I will visit</b> — the sense is <b>'and you will adorn yourself'</b> (ותעד) — a parable of a woman who harlots, who puts the nose-ring on her nose and the jewel on her neck, to beautify herself to find favor in the eyes of the paramour."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:52.709598128Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}